# Implementation Plan — 24-Hour Custom Timelapse Image Selection

## Overview & Analogy
Imagine our system as a digital storage house that creates summary motion films (timelapses) from captured site photos. 
Normally, our daily photo clerk only collects pictures taken during daylight hours (6:00 AM to 6:00 PM). 

When the user turns ON the **"Include 24-hour images"** switch, a dedicated 24-hour photo clerk takes over. This clerk selects photos continuously across the entire day and night (full 24-hour period) for the chosen start and end dates. The selected photos are then delivered directly to our existing film manufacturing line. 

If the 24-hour switch is OFF, the regular daylight photo clerk handles the request exactly as before without any changes.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **No Database Migration Required**: The 24-hour preference will be stored inside the existing configuration settings box (`extra_settings` JSON field) on the timelapse setup card.
> 
> **Seamless Integration**: The video creation engine remains unchanged. Only the photo gathering step receives a specialized 24-hour selection worker when enabled.

